WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.151 --> 00:00:03.680
- So the question is what would
actually happen to your body

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.770
if you really gave up sugar,

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.350
I mean completely, for two weeks?

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.320
Let's take a look at that.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.790
Number one, you are gonna
lose your appetite to sugar.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:14.870
Why?

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.240
Because every time you consume sugar,

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.280
a hormone comes in there and
pushes your blood sugars down,

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.160
causing a low blood sugar situation,

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.480
hypoglycemia, to some degree

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.620
and that is gonna cause
you to crave sugar.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.310
So by getting rid of sugar,

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.030
you get rid of the craving for sugar.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:37.640
Number two, you're gonna be less hungry.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.340
Until you do this, you
won't really fully know,

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.560
but I'm telling you,

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.770
it's the sugar that keeps
you hungry all the time.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.840
When you give up the sugar,
you become a lot less hungry.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:48.673
Why?

00:00:48.673 --> 00:00:51.080
Because you stabilize your blood sugars

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:54.170
and now your cells can be actually fed

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.370
because when you're living on sugar,

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.940
because sugar is toxic to the body,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.690
the body starts rejecting it.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.060
That's called insulin resistance.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.210
So the body is blocking insulin

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.660
because that controls sugar

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.810
and what your body is really trying to do

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:11.350
is limit the amount of
sugar inside the cells.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.090
So the body doesn't
consider it a good thing.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.370
It's a bad thing.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:16.960
So when you give it up,
this thing could reverse.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.710
And not only can you now
absorb proper amounts of fuel.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.900
You'll absorb nutrients a lot better too

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:27.900
because insulin resistance also
blocks nutrients, minerals,

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.500
vitamins, and that's one of
the functions of insulin.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.410
All right, number three.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:33.820
You can have less fatigue

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.060
especially after eating a meal.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.333
When you're eating sugar
on a regular basis,

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:41.870
usually you're gonna
be tired after you eat

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.370
and that is a blood sugar thing.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.203
But you're gonna find

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:46.330
that you're no longer gonna
be that tired after you eat.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:49.780
It just means that now you're
no longer having higher sugar,

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:52.600
which basically makes the brain tired.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.373
It's normal sugar, and now
your brain can be awake.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.620
All right, number four,

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:02.290
